ef 17592186045417] [17592186150821 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186150826 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186150821 #edb/ref 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186150821 #edb/ref 1077 "selection" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186150821 #edb/ref 1078 #edb/ref 17592186150825 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186150821 #edb/ref 1079 #uuid "14edd6b1-b94a-57fc-9aaf-d788b0b6d33e" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186150822 #edb/ref 1080 "64" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186150822 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186150822 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "a00637db-de9b-56ed-a098-59411cde942a" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186150823 #edb/ref 1080 "36" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186150823 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186150823 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "a3a55e44-b375-54dd-a983-e6ed8acae1ae" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186150824 #edb/ref 1080 "120" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186150824 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186150824 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "b92a08bf-50c4-51af-847d-a2e83b44b73f" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186150825 #edb/ref 1080 "144" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186150825 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186150825 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "6922a0cc-0640-5694-b856-0f882a575714" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186150826 #edb/ref 1080 "104" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186150826 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186150826 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "7eea493d-44d4-59ee-941b-3b758b85f0e3" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186151938 #edb/ref 1069 "e-6244" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186151938 #edb/ref 1071 "Let $R = [0,2]\\times [1,3]$ be a region in the $xy$-plane, and let $f(x,y) = x+2y.$\nFurther, let $P$ be a partition of $R,$ where\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{P}_{1}=\\{0,1,2\\},\\,{P}_{2}=\\{1,2,3\\},\\,P={P}_{1}\\times {P}_{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nCalculate the upper Riemann sum $U(f,P).$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186151938 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "e49f7799-2724-5fe0-999f-bfa9ab5ce610" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186151938 #edb/ref 1074 "First, let's draw the region $R$ and the partition $P.$\n\n![](images/4f/4faf932e63a57d2fe53fb3942cfe21c65d0d2a88692c665b2706bd68164855c9.png)\n\nThe upper sum $U(f,P)$ is given by\n\n$$\nU(f,P) = M_{11}\\cdot\\textrm{Area}(R_{11}) + M_{21}\\cdot\\textrm{Area}(R_{21}) + M_{12}\\cdot\\textrm{Area}(R_{12}) + M_{22}\\cdot\\textrm{Area}(R_{22}),\n$$\n\nwhere $M_{ij}$ is the *maximum* value of $f$ in each subregion $R_{ij}.$ We pick the *maximum* value of $f$ because we're finding the *upper* sum,\n\nTaking into account the fact that $\\textrm{Area}(R_{ij})=1$ for all $4$ subregions, the formula for $U(f,P)$ reduces to\n\n$$\nU(f,P) = M_{11} + M_{21} + M_{12} + M_{22}.\n$$\n\nNow, notice that\n\n- $f(x,y) = x+2y$ increases as $x$ increases, and\n\n- $f(x,y) = x+2y$ increases as $y$ increases.\n\n![](images/26/26dc2a5af4c82657d9ec6fa331d4f5bc7575367bd4e3a00a5929b4ecaffe4477.png)\n\nAs a result, the *maximum* value of $f$ in each subregion is attained when we have the *largest* possible $x$ and the *largest* possible $y$. This is the value at the *top right corner* of each subregion.\n\n![](images/6d/6d34737c12c35f6faec5caf37be500ba16c3f7cb18bf5ae660dc6d54182b66da.png)\n\nCalculating the value of $f$ at each top right corner, we get the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{M}_{11} & =f(1,2)=5 \\\\ {M}_{21} & =f(2,2)=6 \\\\ {M}_{12} & =f(1,3)=7 \\\\ {M}_{22} & =f(2,3)=8\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, substituting the above values in our expression for $U,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}U(f,P) & =5+6+7+8=26.\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186151939 #edb/ref 1069 "e-6245" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186151939 #edb/ref 1071 "Let $R = [1,5] \\times [2,6]$ be a region in the $xy$-plane, and let $f(x,y) = 65-x^2-y^2.$\nFurther, let $P$ be a partition of $R,$ where\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{P}_{1}=\\{1,3,5\\},\\,{P}_{2}=\\{2,4,6\\},\\,P={P}_{1}\\times {P}_{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nCalculate the upper Riemann sum $U(f,P).$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186151939 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "1ac785c8-3d14-5968-94d3-6f4588f08d91" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186151939 #edb/ref 1074 "First, let's draw the region $R$ and the partition $P.$\n\n![](images/51/5133b73c3707b87725baeee9a34a64898d33056dab9d7d32ac8cc24dbe772321.png)\n\nThe upper sum $U(f,P)$ is given by\n\n$$\nU(f,P) = M_{11}\\cdot\\textrm{Area}(R_{11}) + M_{21}\\cdot\\textrm{Area}(R_{21}) + M_{12}\\cdot\\textrm{Area}(R_{12}) + M_{22}\\cdot\\textrm{Area}(R_{22}),\n$$\n\nwhere $M_{ij}$ is the *maximum* value of $f$ in each subregion $R_{ij}.$ We pick the *maximum* value of $f$ because we're finding the *upper* sum.\n\nTaking into account the fact that $\\textrm{Area}(R_{ij})=4$ for all $4$ regions, the formula for $U(f,P)$ reduces to\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}U(f,P) & =4\\cdot {M}_{11}+4\\cdot {M}_{21}+4\\cdot {M}_{12}+4\\cdot {M}_{22} \\\\  & =4({M}_{11}+{M}_{21}+{M}_{12}+{M}_{22}).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, notice that\n\n- $f(x,y) = 65-x^2-y^2$ decreases as $x$ increases, and\n\n- $f(x,y) = 65-x^2-y^2$ decreases as $y$ increases.\n\n![](images/5b/5b711e2c33e8966dfc9f4274a8f556f712d51a450bbcd0cadb68771fd050d304.png)\n\nAs a result, the *maximum* value of $f$ in each subregion is attained when we have the *smallest* possible $x$ and the *smallest* possible $y.$ This is the value at the *bottom left corner* of each subregion.\n\n![](images/ad/ad83cf465252b1f880757405ca3ff9ab5e1b9b1e50d712bd3b81305b7973af27.png)\n\nCalculating the value of $f$ at each bottom left corner, we get the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{M}_{11} & =f(1,2)=60 \\\\ {M}_{21} & =f(3,2)=52 \\\\ {M}_{12} & =f(1,4)=48 \\\\ {M}_{22} & =f(3,4)=40\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, substituting the above values in our expression for $U,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}U(f,P) & =4(60+52+48+40)=800.\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186151940 #edb/ref 1069 "e-6246" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186151940 #edb/ref 1071 "![](images/33/33269c79413f4435d074d90cd727f2a53e7b9831300bfcaf0b5a7122df764080.png)\n\nConsider the partition of the rectangular region $R$ shown above and the positive function $f(x,y)$ defined on $R.$ Find an expression for the upper Riemann sum of $f$ with respect to this partition.\n\n*Hint: $M_{ij}$ denotes the maximum value of $f$ on the subregion $R_{ij}$*" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186151940 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "14e77998-b24b-56c1-8901-dc94d3ef98a5" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186151940 #edb/ref 1074 "To calculate the upper Riemann sum $U$ with respect to the given partition, we compute the sum of the volumes of $2$ rectangular solids, one for each $R_{ij}.$\n\nThe volume of the rectangular solid corresponding to each subregion $R_{ij}$ is given by\n\n$$\nM_{ij}\\cdot \\textrm{Area}(R_{ij}).\n$$\n\nwhere $M_{ij}$ denotes the maximum value of $f$ on the subregion $R_{ij}.$ We pick the *maximum* value of $f$ because we're finding the *upper* sum.\n\nSo in our case, we have\n\n$$\nU = M_{11}\\cdot \\textrm{Area}(R_{11}) + M_{21}\\cdot \\textrm{Area}(R_{21}).\n$$\n\nNow, notice that\n\n$$\n\\textrm{Area}(R_{11}) = 8\n$$\n\nand\n\n$$\n\\textrm{Area}(R_{21}) = 4.\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}U & =8\\cdot {M}_{11}+4\\cdot {M}_{21} \\\\  & =8{M}_{11}+4{M}_{21}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186152150 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186152398 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186152150 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186152712 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186152150 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186256779 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186152150 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186345024 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186152150 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186345038 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186152150 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186345040 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186152150 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186345041 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186152150 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186543501 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186152150 #edb/ref 1039 "Calculating an Upper Riemann Sum in the Case of a Strictly Increasing Function" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186152150 #edb/ref 1041 #edb/ref 17592186151938 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186152150 #edb/ref 1042 #uuid "34f7fe39-9ca2-5c27-8852-96eb58a51f62" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186152151 #edb/ref 1037 #edb/ref 17592186048206 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186152151 #edb/ref 1037 #edb/ref 17592186049573 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186152151 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186152713 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186152151 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186152719 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186152151 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186259497 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186152151 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186259498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186152151 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186259499 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186152151 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186345052 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186152151 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186543560 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186152151 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186543569 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186152151 #edb/ref 1039 "Calculating an Upper Riemann Sum in the Case of a Strictly Decreasing Function" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186152151 #edb/ref 1041 #edb/ref 17592186151939 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186152151 #edb/ref 1042 #uuid "4cd571d2-a2d6-534d-84dd-a8182f64d1d6" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186152152 #edb/ref 1037 #edb/ref 17592186048363 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186152152 #edb/ref 1037 #edb/ref 17592186049629 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186152152 #edb/ref 1037 #edb/ref 17592186049878 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186152152 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186152394 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186152152 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186152395 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186152152 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186256773 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186152152 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186256774 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186152152 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186256775 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186152152 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186256776 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186152152 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186543539 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186152152 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186543574 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186152152 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186543585 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186152152 #edb/ref 1039 "Calculating an Expression for the Upper Bound in Terms of Maximum Values" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186152152 #edb/ref 1041 #edb/ref 17592186151940 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186152152 #edb/ref 1042 #uuid "9fa8da8f-00bb-5663-b578-99086398a1b7" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186152326 #edb/ref 1043 #edb/ref 17592186153045 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186152326 #edb/ref 1043 #edb/ref 17592186153046 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186152326 #edb/ref 1043 #edb/ref 17592186153047 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186152326 #edb/ref 1043 #edb/ref 17592186153051 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186152326 #edb/ref 1043 #edb/ref 17592186153183 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186152326 #edb/ref 1043 #edb/ref 17592186153185 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186152326 #edb/ref 1044 #edb/ref 17592186045463 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186152326 #edb/ref 1045 "Approximating Volumes Using Upper Riemann Sums" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186152326 #edb/ref 1046 #edb/ref 17592186153183 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186152326 #edb/ref 1049 #edb/ref 17592186050800 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186152326 #edb/ref 1050 600.0 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186152326 #edb/ref 1053 #uuid "8a4d8167-cbc1-5987-8890-23de47beaf31" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186152395 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186256243 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186152395 #edb/ref 1069 "q-122847" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186152395 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186152395 #edb/ref 1071 "![](images/c2/c28d3a6098da6c8be022974e96b5242e3bed58ef1347d92571b49c7b521a3b0d.png)\n\nConsider the partition of the rectangular region $R$ shown above and the positive function $f(x,y)$ defined on $R.$ Which of the following gives an expression for the upper Riemann sum of $f$ with respect to this partition.\n\n*Hint: ${M}_{ij}$ denotes the maximum value of $f$ on the subregion ${R}_{ij}$*" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186152395 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "3bab7c56-0d70-56a8-b7e8-20549b73d742" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186152395 #edb/ref 1074 "To calculate the upper Riemann sum $U$ with respect to the given partition, we compute the sum of the volumes of $4$ rectangular solids, one for each ${R}_{ij}.$\n\nThe volume of the rectangular solid corresponding to each subregion ${R}_{ij}$ is given by\n\n$$\n{M}_{ij}\\cdot \\text{Area}({R}_{ij}).\n$$\n\nwhere ${M}_{ij}$ denotes the maximum value of $f$ on the subregion ${R}_{ij}.$ We pick the *maximum* value of $f$ because we're finding the *upper* sum.\n\nSo in our case, we have\n\n$$\nU={M}_{11}\\cdot \\text{Area}({R}_{11})+{M}_{21}\\cdot \\text{Area}({R}_{21})+{M}_{12}\\cdot \\text{Area}({R}_{12})+{M}_{22}\\cdot \\text{Area}({R}_{22}).\n$$\n\nNow, notice that\n\n$$\n\\text{Area}({R}_{11})=\\text{Area}({R}_{12})=2\n$$\n\nand\n\n$$\n\\text{Area}({R}_{21})=\\text{Area}({R}_{22})=1.\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}U & =2\\cdot {M}_{11}+{M}_{21}+2\\cdot {M}_{12}+{M}_{22} \\\\  & =2{M}_{11}+{M}_{21}+2{M}_{12}+{M}_{22}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186152398 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186148919 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186152398 #edb/ref 1069 "q-123133" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186152398 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045486 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186152398 #edb/ref 1071 "Let $R=[2,10]\\times [3,7]$ be a region in the $xy$-plane, and let $f(x,y)=x+y.$\nFurther, let $P$ be a partition of $R,$ where\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{P}_{1}=\\{2,6,10\\},\\,{P}_{2}=\\{3,5,7\\},\\,P={P}_{1}\\times {P}_{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nCalculate the upper Riemann sum $U(f,P).$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186152398 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "c4585e46-b2c8-5baf-a8e2-9d0a8e6d3871" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186152398 #edb/ref 1074 "First, let's draw the region $R$ and the partition $P.$\n\n![](images/09/0938d12d93c4f962a4ebd8daa7efe4543fc30c419be7d89f165e21bcadce84bb.png)\n\nThe upper sum $U(f,P)$ is given by\n\n$$\nU(f,P)={M}_{11}\\cdot \\text{Area}({R}_{11})+{M}_{21}\\cdot \\text{Area}({R}_{21})+{M}_{12}\\cdot \\text{Area}({R}_{12})+{M}_{22}\\cdot \\text{Area}({R}_{22}),\n$$\n\nwhere ${M}_{ij}$ is the *maximum* value of $f$ in each subregion ${R}_{ij}.$ We pick the *maximum* value of $f$ because we're finding the *upper* sum.\n\nTaking into account the fact that $\\text{Area}({R}_{ij})=8$ for all $4$ subregions, the formula for $U(f,P)$ reduces to\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}U(f,P) & =8\\cdot {M}_{11}+8\\cdot {M}_{21}+8\\cdot {M}_{12}+8\\cdot {M}_{22} \\\\  & =8({M}_{11}+{M}_{21}+{M}_{12}+{M}_{22}).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, notice that\n\n- $f(x,y)=x+y$ increases as $x$ increases, and\n\n- $f(x,y)=x+y$ increases as $y$ increases.\n\n![](images/af/af324138b21609cef59f49df0920ecc12681b8cb7667a843ff2d3fff3c27ea13.png)\n\nAs a result, the *maximum* value of $f$ in each subregion is attained when we have the *largest* possible $x$ and the *largest* possible $y.$ This is the value at the *top right corner* of each subregion. \n\n![](images/14/14b50472bce6d935803ca4f74bb5b1761903c0b0b015ce72e7e1e5e08f35868b.png)\n\nHence:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{M}_{11} & =f(6,5)=11 \\\\ {M}_{21} & =f(10,5)=15 \\\\ {M}_{12} & =f(6,7)=13 \\\\ {M}_{22} & =f(10,7)=17\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}U(f,P) & =8(11+15+13+17) \\\\  & =448.\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186152712 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186150779 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186152712 #edb/ref 1069 "q-75047" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186152712 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186152712 #edb/ref 1071 "Let $R=[2,4]\\times [2,4]$ be a region in the $xy$-plane, and let $f(x,y)={x}^{2}+{y}^{2}.$\nFurther, let $P$ be a partition of $R,$ where\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{P}_{1}=\\{2,3,4\\},\\,{P}_{2}=\\{2,3,4\\},\\,P={P}_{1}\\times {P}_{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nCalculate the upper Riemann sum $U(f,P).$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186152712 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "122fa252-520a-5995-91e9-6f1ba7a38a89" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186152712 #edb/ref 1074 "First, let's draw the region $R$ and the partition $P.$\n\n![](images/e8/e88b9d4b756f76a8b7c75287f0c4e3ff07f7b458dcdcea703769fc6da56f2a12.png)\n\nThe upper sum $U(f,P)$ is given by\n\n$$\nU(f,P)={M}_{11}\\cdot \\text{Area}({R}_{11})+{M}_{21}\\cdot \\text{Area}({R}_{21})+{M}_{12}\\cdot \\text{Area}({R}_{12})+{M}_{22}\\cdot \\text{Area}({R}_{22}),\n$$\n\nwhere ${M}_{ij}$ is the *maximum* value of $f$ in each subregion ${R}_{ij}.$ We pick the *maximum* value of $f$ because we're finding the *upper* sum.\n\nTaking into account the fact that $\\text{Area}({R}_{ij})=1$ for all $4$ subregions, the formula for $U(f,P)$ reduces to\n\n$$\nU(f,P)={M}_{11}+{M}_{21}+{M}_{12}+{M}_{22}.\n$$\n\nNow, notice that\n\n- $f(x,y)={x}^{2}+{y}^{2}$ increases as $x$ increases, and\n\n- $f(x,y)={x}^{2}+{y}^{2}$ increases as $y$ increases.\n\n![](images/8d/8dc9b8c4634691d17614c39e542488fb17d2918737be0dad5d262cd9a1fd827a.png)\n\nAs a result, the *maximum* value of $f$ in each subregion is attained when we have the *largest* possible $x$ and the *largest* possible $y.$ This is the value at the *top right corner* of each subregion. \n\n![](images/be/beb238668c9c1ebb66f8c7ec3cd8a40b267b47d7ba1cbd2e351c65b3c17d7a84.png)\n\nHence:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{M}_{11} & =f(3,3)=18 \\\\ {M}_{21} & =f(4,3)=25 \\\\ {M}_{12} & =f(3,4)=25 \\\\ {M}_{22} & =f(4,4)=32\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}U(f,P) & =18+25+25+32 \\\\  & =100.\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186152713 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186344546 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186152713 #edb/ref 1069 "q-75048" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186152713 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186152713 #edb/ref 1071 "Let $R=[-1,1]\\times [-1,1]$ be a region in the $xy$-plane, and let $f(x,y)=5-3x-y.$\nFurther, let $P$ be a partition of $R,$ where\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{P}_{1}=\\{-1,0,1\\},\\,{P}_{2}=\\{-1,0,1\\},\\,P={P}_{1}\\times {P}_{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nCalculate the upper Riemann sum $U(f,P).$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186152713 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "06416db6-a5ef-5504-be7c-78a29bd00e0c" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186152713 #edb/ref 1074 "First, let's draw the region $R$ and the partition $P.$\n\n![](images/85/859d9d6b15dbd08b4c015816e46986268f92a94770df866a562f3e379bae5365.png)\n\nThe upper sum $U(f,P)$ is given by\n\n$$\nU(f,P)={M}_{11}\\cdot \\text{Area}({R}_{11})+{M}_{21}\\cdot \\text{Area}({R}_{21})+{M}_{12}\\cdot \\text{Area}({R}_{12})+{M}_{22}\\cdot \\text{Area}({R}_{22}),\n$$\n\nwhere ${M}_{ij}$ is the *maximum* value of $f$ in each subregion ${R}_{ij}.$ We pick the *maximum* value of $f$ because we're finding the *upper* sum.\n\nTaking into account the fact that $\\text{Area}({R}_{ij})=1$ for all $4$ subregions, the formula for $U(f,P)$ reduces to\n\n$$\nU(f,P)={M}_{11}+{M}_{21}+{M}_{12}+{M}_{22}.\n$$\n\nNow, notice that\n\n- $f(x,y)=5-3x-y$ decreases as $x$ increases, and\n\n- $f(x,y)=5-3x-y$ decreases as $y$ increases.\n\n![](images/4c/4c688c7cf529800b8f1ad075dc70784e40a59163330031b375eaad4b1cdd64c9.png)\n\nAs a result, the *maximum* value of $f$ in each subregion is attained when we have the *smallest* possible $x$ and the *smallest* possible $y.$ This is the value at the *bottom left corner* of each subregion.\n\n![](images/62/6269ba3c4fd853fff89327ab9e6968e2f52439f5c86c0ec5a21dce1620d9ba5d.png)\n\nHence:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{M}_{11} & =f(-1,-1)=9 \\\\ {M}_{21} & =f(0,-1)=6 \\\\ {M}_{12} & =f(-1,0)=8 \\\\ {M}_{22} & =f(0,0)=5\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}U(f,P) & =9+6+8+5 \\\\  & =28.\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186152719 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186150821 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186152719 #edb/ref 1069 "q-75229" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186152719 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045486 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186152719 #edb/ref 1071 "Let $R=[-2,2]\\times [-2,2]$ be a region in the $xy$-plane, and let $f(x,y)=6-2x-y.$\nFurther, let $P$ be a partition of $R,$ where\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{P}_{1}=\\{-2,0,2\\},\\,{P}_{2}=\\{-2,0,2\\},\\,P={P}_{1}\\times {P}_{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nCalculate the upper Riemann sum $U(f,P).$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186152719 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "27fbd536-fbac-5629-a345-3477109a83e7" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186152719 #edb/ref 1074 "First, let's draw the region $R$ and the partition $P.$\n\n![](images/c8/c8b7ffacce26030414c0e319624f5c171d28599f0cf9375e40ddaf252d6b7380.png)\n\nThe upper sum $U(f,P)$ is given by\n\n$$\nU(f,P)={M}_{11}\\cdot \\text{Area}({R}_{11})+{M}_{21}\\cdot \\text{Area}({R}_{21})+{M}_{12}\\cdot \\text{Area}({R}_{12})+{M}_{22}\\cdot \\text{Area}({R}_{22})\n$$\n\nwhere ${M}_{ij}$ is the *maximum* value of $f$ in each subregion ${R}_{ij}.$ We pick the *maximum* value of $f$ because we're finding the *upper* sum.\n\nTaking into account the fact that $\\text{Area}({R}_{ij})=4$ for all $4$ subregions, the formula for $U(f,P)$ reduces to\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}U(f,P) & =4\\cdot {M}_{11}+4\\cdot {M}_{21}+4\\cdot {M}_{12}+4\\cdot {M}_{22} \\\\  & =4({M}_{11}+{M}_{21}+{M}_{12}+{M}_{22}).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, notice that\n\n- $f(x,y)=6-2x-y$ decreases as $x$ increases, and\n\n- $f(x,y)=6-2x-y$ decreases as $y$ increases.\n\n![](images/77/770593c18eaaebff55c73151b0e98628bd4ece00b75380b29fde8d1721f1cf16.png)\n\nAs a result, the *maximum* value of $f$ in each subregion is attained when we have the *smallest* possible $x$ and the *smallest* possible $y.$ This is the value at the *bottom left corner* of each subregion.\n\n![](images/8d/8dc8062cb5c436a0135abd2340fcaa39560658c4a23f13f0cb70893789a81836.png)\n\nHence:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{M}_{11} & =f(-2,-2)=12 \\\\ {M}_{21} & =f(0,-2)=8 \\\\ {M}_{12} & =f(-2,0)=10 \\\\ {M}_{22} & =f(0,0)=6\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}U(f,P) & =4(12+8+10+6) \\\\  & =144.\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186153045 #edb/ref 1061 23449 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186153045 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "cf8a0158-b0bb-51d1-a026-029d210bf549" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186153045 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186152150 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186153046 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186153045 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186153046 #edb/ref 1061 23450 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186153046 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "171bad61-0332-58ad-81bd-9b1ee0d315e8" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186153046 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186152151 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186153047 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186153051 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186153047 #edb/ref 1061 23451 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186153047 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "cfacb02d-e3c0-53df-a1ea-8dac614072e6" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186153047 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186152152 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186153051 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186153185 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186153051 #edb/ref 1061 23472 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186153051 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "b0239999-1cf0-5570-9e21-786f635fe397" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186153051 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186153350 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186153183 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186153047 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186153183 #edb/ref 1061 35488 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186153183 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "883dc60d-baeb-5e5a-83a1-e45e3ddfdcfc" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186153183 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186153417 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186153185 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186153046 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186153185 #edb/ref 1061 35509 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186153185 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "32dfda1a-8765-544a-8839-29e132fa4334" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186153185 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186153419 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186153350 #edb/ref 1064 "Recall the region $R$ that we encountered earlier:\n\n![](images/20/2026210e2cd58b2f2f7290a2d4f4186875903d146d02597787393727afd7f6a6.png)\n\nEarlier, we saw that an upper bound for the volume $V$ of \n\n$$\nz = f(x,y) = 3-x^2-y^2\n$$\n\n \n\ndefined over the region $R$ with respect to the partition $P$ (shown above) is given by\n\n$$\nU = \\dfrac14(M_{11} + M_{21}+ M_{12} + M_{22}),\n$$\n\nwhere $M_{ij}$ is the maximum value of $f$ over the subregion $R_{ij}.$ Our goal now is to calculate the values of $M_{ij}.$\n\nWe start by considering $M_{11},$ so let's zoom in on $R_{11}\\mathbin{:}$\n\n![](images/04/042a236318a636de2fbfd9522dd221dbfd47906e63bc2290ca554bbcfccec958.png)\n\nNow, let's take a closer look at the function $f(x,y)\\mathbin{:}$\n\n$$\nf(x,y) = 3-x^2-y^2\n$$\n\n \n\nNotice that\n\n- as we *increase* $x,$ the value of $f$ *decreases* (because we're *subtracting* $x^2$), and\n\n- as we *increase* $y,$ the value of $f$ *decreases* (because we're *subtracting* $y^2$).\n\n![](images/4e/4e29408793329549172cdcc7113ec1d356d5b78e07b59b71e0d5284149375442.png)\n\nAs a result, the *maximum* value of $f$ in this subregion is attained when we have the *smallest* possible $x$ and the *smallest* possible $y.$ This is the value at the *bottom left corner* of the subregion.\n\n![](images/4f/4fb0e98a83794b8e5a105e3b1afaa19bf28be1f8986c958177b2bb3b10f3bb28.png)\n\nSince the function $f(x,y)$ decreases as $x$ and $y$ increase everywhere on $R,$ the maximum value of $f$ in each subregion $R_{ij}$ *always* occurs at the bottom left corner! \n\n![](images/aa/aaeb4af429c9509b05377954d7c114fd19098477065cceb92b219c6e62703671.png)\n\nCalculating the value of $f$ at each bottom left corner, we get the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{M}_{11} & =f(0,0)=3 \\\\ {M}_{21} & =f(\\frac{1}{2},0)=2.75 \\\\ {M}_{12} & =f(0,\\frac{1}{2})=2.75 \\\\ {M}_{22} & =f(\\frac{1}{2},\\frac{1}{2})=2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, substituting the above values in our expression for $U,$ we get\n\n$$\nU = \\dfrac14(3+2.75+2.75+2.5) = 2.75.\n$$\n\nRemember that $U$ is the *upper* Riemann sum, which is an *upper* bound for the volume between $z=f(x,y)$ and the region $R.$ Therefore, we conclude that the volume between $z = f(x,y)$ and the region $R$ must be smaller than (or equal to) $2.75.$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186153350 #edb/ref 1065 3957 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186153350 #edb/ref 1066 #uuid "2abddec2-887d-532c-8ebc-62149543755e" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186153350 #edb/ref 1067 "Calculating the Maximum Value of the Function in Each Partition" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186153417 #edb/ref 1064 "In this lesson, we will describe a process for calculating an **upper bound** for the volume enclosed between a surface $z=f(x,y)$ and the $xy$-plane. \n\nAs an example, consider the rectangle $R$ in the $xy$-plane, defined as\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}R=\\{(x,y)\\,:\\,0\\le x\\le 1,\\,0\\le y\\le 1\\}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nA sketch of the region $R$ is shown below.\n\n![](images/bf/bf7ef4752b0910b5544707eef97c854d8eeeedbc221a81c5fa631cf38b8b8d9a.png)\n\nNow consider the function $f(x,y) = 3-x^2-y^2,$ defined over $R,$ shown below.\n\n![](images/34/34f7936b29e6a177ae0c831e36654dc5059514580a1947324a40d52320b83e5a.png)\n\nThe space underneath the surface and above the region $R$ defines a fixed volume $V.$ Our goal is to find an upper bound for $V.$ We do this by approximating this volume using rectangular solids. \n\nWe start by partitioning the $x$- and $y$-intervals of $R.$ Let's pick two subintervals of equal length for both $x$ and $y.$\n\n![](images/c3/c375b605ca6b7d7f2935218976f5e09db5ed2cfb64d811b1fe0a854d02646a36.png)\n\nThe region $R$ is now partitioned into $4$ rectangles:\n\n![](images/20/2026210e2cd58b2f2f7290a2d4f4186875903d146d02597787393727afd7f6a6.png)\n\nWe seek an *upper* bound for the volume $V.$ So, we let $M_{ij}$ be the *largest* value of $f$ in each subregion $R_{ij}.$ We then define a rectangular solid in each subregion whose base is $R_{ij}$ and whose height is $M_{ij}.$ \n\nFor example, the rectangular solid corresponding to $R_{11}$ is given below. \n\n![](images/62/62cee54b71235dc75cab863f0971735ec221fc61a022edf78994ea3f935c1cd4.png)\n\nThe volume of this rectangular solid is\n\n$$\nM_{11}\\cdot \\textrm{Area}(R_{11})  = \\dfrac14M_{11}.\n$$\n\nSimilarly, the volumes of the rectangular solids formed by the partitions $R_{21}, R_{12},$ and $R_{22}$ respectively are\n\n$$\n\\dfrac14M_{21}, \\qquad \\dfrac14M_{12}, \\qquad \\dfrac14M_{22}.\n$$\n\nDrawing all four rectangular solids, we get a volume that looks as follows:\n\n![](images/f8/f8f44d8a180838cb2b79b775483260ea9a30608cb8a618eaf86a5edcabd2c610.png)\n\nThe upper bound $U$ for our volume is the sum of the volumes of our four rectangular solids. This gives\n\n$$\nU = \\dfrac14(M_{11} + M_{21} + M_{12} + M_{22}).\n$$\n\nThe number $U$ is called the **upper Riemann sum with respect to the given partition**.\n\n**Note:** We don't yet know the values of $M_{ij},$ the height of each solid. We'll learn to figure these out a little later in the lesson. For now, we will just focus on writing $U$ as an expression of $M_{ij}.$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186153417 #edb/ref 1065 5777 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186153417 #edb/ref 1066 #uuid "aca556d7-abe9-5c2e-a21c-a1abde3b1b37" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186153417 #edb/ref 1067 "Introduction" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186153419 #edb/ref 1064 "We need to introduce just a bit more notation. To help us, let's consider the region $R$ and the partition $P$ shown below.\n\n![](images/5d/5d5af7cb2f2b12a52bb624d12938aafd2d34b079ad5d28dc44133292b98956ec.png)\n\nIt's convenient to express our region $R$ in a way that does not involve a diagram. We can do this using the Cartesian product.\n\nUsing the Cartesian product, we have $R = [1,4]\\times [1,3].$\n\nSimilarly:\n\n- The partition of the $x$-interval $[1,4]$ can be expressed as $P_1 = \\{1,2,3,4\\}.$\n\n- The partition of the $y$-interval $[1,3]$ can be expressed as $P_2 = \\{1,3\\}.$\n\n- Therefore, we can write the partition as $P = P_1\\times P_2.$\n\nFinally, we write $U(f,P)$ for the upper Riemann sum of the function $f$ with respect to $P.$\n\n**Note:** We write $U(f,P)$ because the answer we get for the upper bound $U$ depends on the function $f$ and the partition $P$ that we choose. If we choose a different function or partition, then we'll get a different upper bound." #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186153419 #edb/ref 1065 5783 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186153419 #edb/ref 1066 #uuid "5627ca82-fd4e-522e-abb5-8d82d82137eb" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186153419 #edb/ref 1067 "Updating Our Notation" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186253782 #edb/ref 1080 "{M}_{11}+{M}_{21}+{M}_{31}" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186253782 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186253782 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "0d19970f-bec7-5c20-b651-c4d0064d68a4" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186254488 #edb/ref 1080 "90" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186254488 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186254488 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "5c582835-b1b3-5186-81fd-6f865e65bee2" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186254693 #edb/ref 1080 "{M}_{11}\\cdot {M}_{21}\\cdot {M}_{12}\\cdot {M}_{22}" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186254693 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186254693 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "73cfd878-a98b-5b6c-9768-415ec883dbbb" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186254797 #edb/ref 1080 "6{M}_{11}+2{M}_{21}+4{M}_{31}" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186254797 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186254797 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "7f76ae9c-4d43-5dd2-b923-6b7da279bd70" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186254835 #edb/ref 1080 "3{M}_{11}+{M}_{21}+2{M}_{31}" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186254835 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186254835 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "83204b2d-b8b3-5b6d-9928-ddea07e11ab8" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186254837 #edb/ref 1080 "{M}_{11}+3{M}_{21}+2{M}_{31}" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186254837 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186254837 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "832c78c0-5f67-50ca-94e6-c941a28b95ac" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186254941 #edb/ref 1080 "900" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186254941 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186254941 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "90d2434c-de15-5c77-97e7-de9a107f4cc7" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186255068 #edb/ref 1080 "320" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186255068 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186255068 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "9ec8bffa-dd97-56c0-8381-ae4c75c4d634" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186255085 #edb/ref 1080 "48{M}_{11}\\cdot {M}_{21}\\cdot {M}_{31}" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186255085 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186255085 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "a125559f-9ad1-5393-b453-387d4afbbf6f" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186255240 #edb/ref 1080 "{M}_{11}-{M}_{21}+{M}_{12}-{M}_{22}" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186255240 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186255240 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "b2789144-b138-5b29-8c59-3cd2f01c8608" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186255250 #edb/ref 1080 "2({M}_{11}+{M}_{21}+{M}_{12}+{M}_{22})" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186255250 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186255250 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "b318e2a5-8a46-5471-a605-38962b9183ee" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186255474 #edb/ref 1080 "{M}_{11}+{M}_{21}+{M}_{12}+{M}_{22}" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186255474 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186255474 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "cb1c3971-07ec-5035-aa02-5ecbed3c3494" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186255486 #edb/ref 1080 "45" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186255486 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186255486 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "cc5d3bc0-2146-53e7-bbc1-4880587e1249" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186255810 #edb/ref 1080 "2{M}_{11}+{M}_{21}+2{M}_{12}+{M}_{22}" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186255810 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186255810 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "f46a4e73-f0dd-51bd-ab04-3849b4463901" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186255852 #edb/ref 1080 "450" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186255852 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186255852 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "f93feeae-79c1-5460-b446-177cf4275390" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186256029 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186253782 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186256029 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186254797 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186256029 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186254835 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186256029 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186254837 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186256029 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186255085 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186256029 #edb/ref 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186256029 #edb/ref 1077 "selection" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186256029 #edb/ref 1078 #edb/ref 17592186254797 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186256029 #edb/ref 1079 #uuid "3ae87587-d56d-5c95-b689-726e82283fb6" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186256243 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186254693 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186256243 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186255240 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186256243 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186255250 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186256243 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186255474 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186256243 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186255810 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186256243 #edb/ref 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186256243 #edb/ref 1077 "selection" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186256243 #edb/ref 1078 #edb/ref 17592186255810 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186256243 #edb/ref 1079 #uuid "b112ebe7-07df-5f7c-8dd0-20f37949ebb5" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186256317 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186254488 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186256317 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186254941 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186256317 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186255068 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186256317 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186255486 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186256317 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186255852 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186256317 #edb/ref 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186256317 #edb/ref 1077 "selection" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186256317 #edb/ref 1078 #edb/ref 17592186254941 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186256317 #edb/ref 1079 #uuid "deb902b7-3b48-5516-ad6d-401a1adec65e" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186256773 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186256029 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186256773 #edb/ref 1069 "q-123049" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186256773 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186256773 #edb/ref 1071 "![](images/76/76654da8bebc4a156a55bcb6cc7411f4977dfa14634fbceb6e1a7f8e32b2d5b0.png)\n\nConsider the partition of the rectangular region $R$ shown above and the positive function $f(x,y)$ defined on $R.$ Which of the following gives an expression for the upper Riemann sum of $f$ with respect to this partition.\n\n*Hint: ${M}_{ij}$ denotes the maximum value of $f$ on the subregion ${R}_{ij}$*" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186256773 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "df57e019-b35b-55c6-b523-1f5636c88e0f" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186256773 #edb/ref 1074 "To calculate the upper Riemann sum $U$ with respect to the given partition, we compute the sum of the volumes of $3$ rectangular solids, one for each ${R}_{ij}.$\n\nThe volume of the rectangular solid corresponding to each subregion ${R}_{ij}$ is given by\n\n$$\n{M}_{ij}\\cdot \\text{Area}({R}_{ij}).\n$$\n\nwhere ${M}_{ij}$ denotes the maximum value of $f$ on the subregion ${R}_{ij}.$ We pick the *maximum* value of $f$ because we're finding the *upper* sum.\n\nSo in our case, we have\n\n$$\nU={M}_{11}\\cdot \\text{Area}({R}_{11})+{M}_{21}\\cdot \\text{Area}({R}_{21})+{M}_{31}\\cdot \\text{Area}({R}_{31}).\n$$\n\nNow, notice that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{Area}({R}_{11})=6, \\\\ \\text{Area}({R}_{21})=2,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nand\n\n$$\n\\text{Area}({R}_{31})=4.\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}U & =6\\cdot {M}_{11}+2\\cdot {M}_{21}+4\\cdot {M}_{31} \\\\  & =6{M}_{11}+2{M}_{21}+4{M}_{31}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186256779 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186256317 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186256779 #edb/ref 1069 "q-123132" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186256779 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045486 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186256779 #edb/ref 1071 "Let $R=[1,7]\\times [1,6]$ be a region in the $xy$-plane, and let $f(x,y)=xy.$\nFurther, let $P$ be a partition of $R,$ where\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{P}_{1}=\\{1,3,5,7\\},\\,{P}_{2}=\\{1,6\\},\\,P={P}_{1}\\times {P}_{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nCalculate the upper Riemann sum $U(f,P).$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186256779 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "e4225c9b-f9c3-509c-8faa-46e65d5c864c" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186256779 #edb/ref 1074 "First, let's draw the region $R$ and the partition $P.$\n\n![](images/68/68270610704b1ef132469193e7948f54e548fa22223b6fc49b693753f998f874.png)\n\nThe upper sum $U(f,P)$ is given by\n\n$$\nU(f,P)={M}_{11}\\cdot \\text{Area}({R}_{11})+{M}_{21}\\cdot \\text{Area}({R}_{21})+{M}_{31}\\cdot \\text{Area}({R}_{31}),\n$$\n\nwhere ${M}_{ij}$ is the *maximum* value of $f$ in each subregion ${R}_{ij}.$ We pick the *maximum* value of $f$ because we're finding the *upper* sum.\n\nTaking into account the fact that $\\text{Area}({R}_{ij})=10$ for all $3$ subregions, the formula for $U(f,P)$ reduces to\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}U(f,P) & =10\\cdot {M}_{11}+10\\cdot {M}_{21}+10\\cdot {M}_{31} \\\\  & =10({M}_{11}+{M}_{21}+{M}_{31}).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, notice that\n\n- $f(x,y)=xy$ increases as $x$ increases, and\n\n- $f(x,y)=xy$ increases as $y$ increases.\n\n![](images/76/7611c64cc460db725893156f6043644b34962a04f2aacef0b19cf99c5769cda3.png)\n\nAs a result, the *maximum* value of $f$ in each subregion is attained when we have the *largest* possible $x$ and the *largest* possible $y.$ This is the value at the *top right corner* of each subregion.\n\n![](images/75/75f378700ce6593a7ed9577b34e093cbbfe702e9512e9962e0d6f7f681694842.png)\n\nHence:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{M}_{11} & =f(3,6)=18 \\\\ {M}_{21} & =f(5,6)=30 \\\\ {M}_{31} & =f(7,6)=42\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}U(f,P) & =10(18+30+42) \\\\  & =900.\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186343063 #edb/ref 1080 "84" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186343063 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186343063 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "6166967f-21cd-5401-8c32-563682cb17fc" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186343175 #edb/ref 1080 "30" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186343175 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186343175 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "6d5155d4-5040-517e-8e8f-7971ed434882" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186343200 #edb/ref 1080 "24" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186343200 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186343200 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "6fe7d86e-6a6d-5c6e-bae8-62d02e24d8cb" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186343213 #edb/ref 1080 "48" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186343213 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186343213 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "71645f0c-15cc-51be-8849-56f4420f30a1" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186343267 #edb/re